Project at a glance
quantlens is a GPT-2 small inference engine written from scratch in PyTorch, used to measure where int8 quantization hurts the model and whether a rescaling fix repairs it.
Formal title: Where Does Int8 Break? A From-Scratch GPT-2 Inference Engine and Quantization Failure Analysis
Research question: Which layers and activation channels cause int8 quantization error in GPT-2 small, and does a SmoothQuant-style rescaling recover the lost perplexity?
Item
Decision
Model
GPT-2 small, 124M parameters
Language and framework
Python, PyTorch (CPU build)
Evaluation data
WikiText-2 test set, measured as perplexity
Hardware
Laptop CPU, no GPU needed (my estimate: slow but workable)
Duration
5 to 6 weeks part-time (estimate)
Deliverables
Public repo, pytest suite, saved benchmark results, 3 to 4 page report, README with architecture diagram
Why this project
Independent of TrackML and the energy-research work, not data analytics, and it shows engineering and diagnosis together

